WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:03.389
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here!

00:00:03.389 --> 00:00:07.839
Marvel continues its tradition of teasing
us upcoming movies in the MCU with two extra

00:00:07.839 --> 00:00:10.070
scenes in Doctor Strange's credits.

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:14.230
In this video, I'm going to break down the
movie's mid-credits scene and explain some

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:15.420
of its easter eggs.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:20.529
And just to be very clear, there are spoilers
for both Doctor Strange itself and an upcoming

00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:22.130
Marvel movie in this video.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:27.150
So, if you want to avoid those, you can watch
my spoiler-free review of Doctor Strange here,

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.539
and come back and watch this video after you've
seen the movie!

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:34.230
OK, after the initial fancy set of credits
roll, we get a funny scene between Doctor

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:38.010
Strange and Thor who are sitting in Strange's
Sanctum Sanctorum in New York.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.560
Thor comments that Earth now has wizards.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:44.340
Strange then offers Thor a cup of tea, but
Thor refuses saying he doesn't drink tea,

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.210
and Strange magically makes a very large glass
of beer appear instead!

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:51.930
This moment is a nice callback to the scene
in the first Thor movie where the Asgardian

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:55.480
god and Erik Selvig drink a boilermaker in
a bar from a similar sized glass.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:59.890
And, of course, we also know from that movie
that it's coffee that Thor likes, not tea.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:02.210
But what is Thor doing with Doctor Strange
here?

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:06.060
Well, if you think back to the last time we
saw Thor, it was at the end of Avengers: Age

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:10.560
of Ultron when he left the Avengers saying
he was going back to Asgard to investigate

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.429
the visions he had of the Infinity Stones.

00:01:12.429 --> 00:01:16.689
Well, it's likely that Thor heard about what
Strange did in this movie and might even be

00:01:16.689 --> 00:01:19.170
aware that he has access to the Time Stone.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:23.649
This meeting between the two characters links
to the Thor: Ragnarok set photo that was tweeted

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:28.479
showing Chris Hemsworth holding up a card
that reads "177A Bleecker Street" which is

00:01:28.479 --> 00:01:30.729
the address of Doctor Strange's Sanctum Santorum.

00:01:30.729 --> 00:01:35.229
So, back to the mid-credits scene, Strange
explains to Thor that he keeps a watch-list

00:01:35.229 --> 00:01:38.859
of individuals and beings from other realms
that could be a threat to Earth, and he points

00:01:38.859 --> 00:01:42.830
out that Thor's brother Loki is on that list,
and Thor agrees that Loki is indeed a worthy

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:43.850
inclusion on the list.

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:48.650
Something of course we know ourselves from
all the shenanigans Loki's got up to so far,

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:53.090
particularly the events of the Avengers movie
Strange then asks, "why bring [Loki] to New

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:57.020
York?", to which Thor replies that he and
Loki are looking for their father Odin.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:00.979
Strange asks Thor if they find Odin, whether
they'll all return to Asgard promptly.

00:02:00.979 --> 00:02:04.079
Thor agrees that they will, so Strange confirms
he'll help him.

00:02:04.079 --> 00:02:08.330
To understand this scene best we need to roll
back to the events of Thor: The Dark World

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:13.239
and remember that at the very end of that
movie, Loki has taken over the throne in Asgard,

00:02:13.239 --> 00:02:14.760
masquerading as Odin.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:19.629
Since that film, even though Thor appeared
in Age of Ultron, it still hasn't been revealed

00:02:19.629 --> 00:02:24.049
that Thor knows what Loki has been up to,
even though we the audience do know.

00:02:24.049 --> 00:02:28.370
Which suggests that this mid-credits scene
is a snippet of a scene from Thor: Ragnarok

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:32.650
rather than a separate stand-alone scene shot
just for the Doctor Strange movie.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:37.550
After all, this scene was filmed by Ragnarok
director Taika Waititi, rather than Doctor

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:38.620
Strange director Scott Derrickson.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:42.650
I think the last time this happened was with
the post-credits scene for Ant-Man which teased

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:46.620
a short clip with Bucky, Captain America and
Falcon from Captain America: Civil War.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:50.989
All of this means that it looks like Thor
is going to uncover Loki's ruse back on Asgard

00:02:50.989 --> 00:02:54.840
early on in Thor: Ragnarok and that they will
then team up with Doctor Strange to search

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:55.840
for the missing Odin.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:59.730
And it also confirms that as well as Doctor
Strange appearing in Avengers: Infinity War

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:04.920
in 2018, we'll be seeing Benedict Cumberbatch
back in another Marvel movie in 2017.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:09.290
So, that was the mid-credits scene from Doctor
Strange, which I thought was good fun and

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.510
a nice tease for 2017's Thor movie.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:16.250
I especially liked the way Thor's beer glass
kept filling up by magic with more beer!

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:17.849
Must get myself one of those glasses!

00:03:17.849 --> 00:03:22.560
But now, I'd love to know what you think about
Doctor Strange teaming up with Thor next year

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:23.560
in Ragnarok?

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:26.730
And let me know if you've got any predictions
about what we'll see them get up to.

